<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 26.56 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 26.56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 69 basis points to 26.56 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY    27.25 pct    26.56 pct		-69 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY    26.55 pct    26.11 pct		-44 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY   25.60 pct    25.39 pct		-21 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR    25.75 pct    25.34 pct		-41 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1930 EST.</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
